1
00:05:19,090 --> 00:05:25,090
Kama Sutra: A Tale of Love is a drama, history,
romance film directed by Mira Nair.

2
00:10:38,181 --> 00:10:44,181
Tara and Maya are inseparable, with the same tastes, habits, and hobbies.

3
00:15:57,272 --> 00:16:03,272
Years later, the two have matured but have maintained their friendship.

4
00:21:16,363 --> 00:21:22,363
Tara marries local prince Raj Singh, who succeeds the throne as the sole heir.

5
00:26:35,454 --> 00:26:41,454
After the marriage, Raj seeks another female to satisfy his sexual desires, with his sights
settling on Maya, putting a perhaps unforgivable strain on a longtime friendship.

6
00:31:54,545 --> 00:32:00,545
Maya, played by Indira Varma.

7
00:37:13,636 --> 00:37:19,636
Tara, the Queen, played by Sarita Choudhury.

8
00:42:32,727 --> 00:42:38,727
Jai Kumar, played by Ramon Tikaram.

9
00:47:51,818 --> 00:47:57,818
Raj Singh, played by Naveen Andrews.

10
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
Rasa Devi, teacher of the Kama Sutra, played by Rekha.

11
00:58:29,999 --> 00:58:35,999
Biki, played by Khalid Tyabji.

12
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:55,090
Kama Sutra: A Tale of Love is a 1996 historical erotic romance film
co-written, co-produced, and directed by Mira Nair.

13
01:09:08,181 --> 01:09:14,181
The first portion of the film is based on "Utran" ("Hand Me Downs"), a
short story in Urdu by the Indian writer Wajida Tabassum.

14
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
The film takes its title from the ancient Hindu text, the Kama
Sutra but has no relationship with the text.

15
01:19:46,363 --> 01:19:52,363
It stars Naveen Andrews, Sarita Choudhury, Ramon
Tikaram, Rekha and Indira Varma.

16
01:25:05,454 --> 01:25:11,454
The English-language film was produced by Indian,
British, German and Japanese studios.

17
01:30:24,545 --> 01:30:30,545
Declan Quinn won the 1998 Independent Spirit Award for Best
Cinematography for his work in the film.

18
01:35:43,636 --> 01:35:49,636
Kama Sutra was nominated for the Golden Seashell award at the 1996 San Sebastián
International Film Festival and was screened at the Cannes Film Festival.

19
01:41:02,727 --> 01:41:08,727
The film generated controversy at the time of its release and was
banned in India due to its erotic theme and sexual content.

20
01:46:21,818 --> 01:46:27,818
The film explores themes of poetry, eroticism, seduction, india, woman director.

21
01:51:40,909 --> 01:51:46,909
The tone is emotional.
